Q: How to make a column sortable in bootstrap 4 table A: <p>Updated the script tag and initialized var $table = $('#table') now it is working</p>

<pre><code>    &lt;script&gt;
  var $table = $('#table')

  $(function() {
    var data = [
      {
        'id': 0,
        'name': 'Item 0',
        'price': '$0'
      },
      {
        'id': 1,
        'name': 'Item 1',
        'price': '$1'
      },
      {
        'id': 2,
        'name': 'Item 2',
        'price': '$2'
      },
      {
        'id': 3,
        'name': 'Item 3',
        'price': '$3'
      },
      {
        'id': 4,
        'name': 'Item 4',
        'price': '$4'
      },
      {
        'id': 5,
        'name': 'Item 5',
        'price': '$5'
      }
    ]
    $table.bootstrapTable({data: data})
  })
&lt;/script&gt;
</code></pre>

Q: http error 413.1 - request entity too large in .net Core A: <p>If your are using .net core 3.1 or lower,try to add the codes in your startup class:</p>
<pre><code>services.Configure&lt;IISServerOptions&gt;(options =&gt;
{
    options.MaxRequestBodySize = 2147483648;
});
</code></pre>
<p>The official document:<a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/aspnet/core/mvc/models/file-uploads?view=aspnetcore-3.1#iis-1" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/aspnet/core/mvc/models/file-uploads?view=aspnetcore-3.1#iis-1</a></p>
